  <article class="content">
    <h1>Styling</h1>
    <p class="lead">Style your components with scoped CSS. Styles are automatically isolated to prevent conflicts and enable tree-shaking.</p>

    <section id="scoped">
      <h2>Scoped Styles</h2>
      <p>By default, all styles in a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block are scoped to the component.</p>
      
      <div class="demo-box">
        <div class="demo-label">Component A</div>
        <div class="demo-content">
          <button class="demo-btn-a">Primary Button</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="demo-box">
        <div class="demo-label">Component B (same class name, different styles)</div>
        <div class="demo-content">
          <button class="demo-btn-b">Primary Button</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="label">Scoped CSS Example</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;!-- ComponentA.pulse --&gt;
&lt;button class="btn"&gt;Click Me&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
  .btn {
    background: #6b46c1;
    color: white;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;!-- ComponentB.pulse --&gt;
&lt;button class="btn"&gt;Different Button&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
  .btn {
    background: #ef4444;
    color: white;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;!-- Both use ".btn" but styles don't conflict! --&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="info-box">
        <h4>🔒 How Scoping Works</h4>
        <p>Pulse adds a unique hash to each component's selectors (e.g., <code>.btn[data-p-abc123]</code>), preventing style conflicts between components.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="global">
      <h2>Global Styles</h2>
      <p>Use <code>:global()</code> to apply styles globally.</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="label">Global Selectors</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;style&gt;
  /* Global body styles */
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    background: #f9fafb;
  }
  
  /* Global reset */
  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  
  /* Global utility classes */
  :global(.container) {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 20px;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>CSS Variables</h3>
      <div class="code-block">
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;style&gt;
  :global(:root) {
    /* Colors */
    --primary: #6b46c1;
    --primary-dark: #5a3ba8;
    --secondary: #e5e7eb;
    --text: #374151;
    --text-muted: #6b7280;
    
    /* Spacing */
    --spacing-sm: 8px;
    --spacing-md: 16px;
    --spacing-lg: 24px;
    
    /* Radii */
    --radius-sm: 4px;
    --radius-md: 8px;
    --radius-lg: 16px;
  }
  
  .btn {
    background: var(--primary);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  
  .btn:hover {
    background: var(--primary-dark);
  }
&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="dynamic">
      <h2>Dynamic Styles</h2>
      <p>Use expressions to apply styles dynamically based on state.</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="label">Dynamic Classes</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;script&gt;
  const [isActive, setIsActive] = createSignal(false);
  const [size, setSize] = createSignal('medium');
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;!-- Ternary for conditional class --&gt;
&lt;button class={isActive() ? 'btn active' : 'btn'}&gt;
  Toggle Me
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;!-- Template literal for dynamic class --&gt;
&lt;button class={`btn btn-${size()}`}&gt;
  Sized Button
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
  .btn { padding: 10px 20px; }
  .btn.active { background: #10b981; }
  .btn-small { padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .btn-medium { padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 1rem; }
  .btn-large { padding: 14px 28px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>Inline Styles</h3>
      <div class="code-block">
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;script&gt;
  const [width, setWidth] = createSignal(50);
  const [color, setColor] = createSignal('#6b46c1');
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;!-- Dynamic inline styles --&gt;
&lt;div 
  class="progress-bar"
  style={`width: ${width()}%; background: ${color()}`}
&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;input 
  type="range" 
  min="0" 
  max="100" 
  value={width}
  onInput={e => setWidth(e.target.value)}
/&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="best-practices">
      <h2>Best Practices</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Practice</th>
            <th>Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Use Scoped Styles</td>
            <td>Keep styles inside components for isolation</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>CSS Variables</td>
            <td>Define design tokens globally for consistency</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Avoid !important</td>
            <td>Scoping eliminates specificity wars</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Semantic Classes</td>
            <td>Name classes descriptively (.card, .header)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Mobile First</td>
            <td>Start with mobile styles, add breakpoints up</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  </article>
</main>

